Preparing the Function-Word Matrix
We use the 200 most frequent words in the combined corpus as features — a standard approach in stylometry that captures predominantly function words.


Code
set.seed(2026)

# Sample equal-length chunks: 3 chunks of 1000 lines per book
chunk_size &lt;- 1000

books_chunked &lt;- books |&gt;
    dplyr::group_by(book) |&gt;
    dplyr::mutate(chunk_id = ceiling(dplyr::row_number() / chunk_size)) |&gt;
    dplyr::filter(chunk_id &lt;= 3) |&gt;          # keep at most 3 chunks per book
    dplyr::mutate(
        doc_id = paste0(book, "_chunk", chunk_id)
