Exercises: Text Summarisation






Q12. You summarise 200 abstracts and find that about 20% of summaries begin with “Here is a one-sentence summary:” despite your prompt saying “Do not include any preamble.” What is the most robust fix?





Use a larger model — 3B models cannot follow formatting instructions




Add post-processing to remove common preamble patterns with str_remove(), and strengthen the prompt with an example of the desired format: 'Example output: This study investigates...'. Showing the model what the output should look like (few-shot prompting) is more reliable than negative instructions alone.




Use chat() instead of generate() — it follows formatting instructions more reliably




Switch output = 'text' to output = 'df' — this strips preamble automatically
